# Outer and inner products: APL ∘.f and f.g; K's each-left x f\: y.

=== times-table
apl: (1+⍳3)∘.×1+⍳4
k: (1+!3)*\:1+!4
py: mat([[i * j for j in range(1, 5)] for i in range(1, 4)])

=== outer-compare
apl: 1 2 3∘.<1 2 3
k: 1 2 3<\:1 2 3
py: mat([[T if i < j else Fa for j in (1, 2, 3)] for i in (1, 2, 3)])

=== outer-scalar
apl: 2∘.+1 2
py: vec(3, 4)

=== outer-rank3
apl: (2 2⍴1)∘.+1 2
k: (2 2#1)+\:1 2
refuse: KR_E_RANK

=== hilbert-4
apl: ÷1+(⍳4)∘.+⍳4
k: recip 1+(!4)+\:!4
py: mat([[F(1, i + j + 1) for j in range(4)] for i in range(4)])

=== hilbert-row-sums-8
apl: +/÷1+(⍳8)∘.+⍳8
py: vec(*[foldr("add", [F(1, i + j + 1) for j in range(8)]) for i in range(8)])

=== matrix-product
apl: (2 2⍴1 2 3 4)+.×2 2⍴5 6 7 8
canon: (inner add mul (reshape (vec 2 2) (vec 1 2 3 4)) (reshape (vec 2 2) (vec 5 6 7 8)))
py: mat([[19, 22], [43, 50]])

=== matrix-vector
apl: (2 3⍴⍳6)+.×1 1 1
py: vec(3, 12)

=== vector-matrix
apl: 1 1+.×2 3⍴⍳6
py: vec(3, 5, 7)

=== vector-dot
apl: 1r2 1r3+.×2 3
py: F(2)

=== inner-max-min
apl: (2 2⍴1 5 3 2)⌈.⌊2 2⍴4 1 2 6
py: m_inner("max", "min", mat([[1, 5], [3, 2]]), mat([[4, 1], [2, 6]]))

=== inner-and-eq
apl: (2 2⍴1 2 3 4)∧.=2 2⍴1 3 2 4
py: m_inner("and", "eq", mat([[1, 2], [3, 4]]), mat([[1, 3], [2, 4]]))

=== inner-length
apl: (2 3⍴⍳6)+.×1 2
refuse: KR_E_LENGTH

=== inner-scalar
apl: 2+.×1 2
refuse: KR_E_RANK

=== hilbert-inverse-check
apl: h←÷1+(⍳3)∘.+⍳3 ⋄ hi←3 3⍴9 ¯36 30 ¯36 192 ¯180 30 ¯180 180 ⋄ h+.×hi
py: mat([[1, 0, 0], [0, 1, 0], [0, 0, 1]])

=== matrix-power-overflow
apl: m←2 2⍴3037000500 0 0 1 ⋄ m+.×m
refuse: ZXV_E_RANGE
